               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 55-year-old female, who presented on 06/01/1981 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Laboratory investigations confirmed elevated inflammatory markers, and abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was resuscitated with intravenous fluids and commenced on antibiotic therapy. Given the clinical picture, she underwent laparoscopic appendectomy on 07/01/1981, which was performed without complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and the patient was mobilised early with physiotherapy support. She was discharged home on 09/01/1981 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks. Should you have any questions, do not hesitate to contact me.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
